    <string name="about_what_title">What is Acadex?</string>
    <string name="about_what_body">Acadex is a student-built academic knowledge archive designed to make learning materials accessible, organized, and searchable for every student. Inspired by the gap in access to quality reviewers and study resources, Acadex lets students upload, share, and discover notes, PDFs, presentations, and practice quizzes — all organized by subject and indexed for easy retrieval.</string>
    <string name="about_philosophy_title">Our Philosophy</string>
    <string name="about_philosophy_body">\"Information becomes education when it is organized.\" Acadex is built on the belief that knowledge shared is knowledge multiplied. Every submission to the archive makes the next student\'s study session a little easier.</string>
    <string name="about_can_do_title">What you can do</string>
    <string name="about_can_do_body">Upload PDFs, Word documents, PowerPoint files, and images. Browse and search the full archive by subject. Save materials to your personal Saved Index. Take practice quizzes and track your history. Rate and comment on materials to help surface the best content. AI-powered summarization and quiz generation coming soon.</string>
    <string name="about_coming_title">Coming Soon</string>
    <string name="about_coming_body">Firebase cloud storage for persistent uploads across devices. In-app PDF and document viewer. AI Summarizer — instant summaries and auto-generated quizzes from uploaded files. Cross-device sync and user accounts with full history.</string>
    <string name="about_built_title">Built by</string>
    <string name="about_built_body">Acadex was created as a capstone project to demonstrate how structured academic tooling can close the resource gap among students. Developed with Kotlin on Android, backed by Firebase Authentication and Supabase.</string>
    <string name="about_footer">© 2025 Acadex. All rights reserved. This is a student project and is not affiliated with any academic institution.</string>
